cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis, please cite it as below."
title: "AON single-nucleus RNA-seq: molecular characterization of Anterior Olfactory Nucleus glutamatergic populations"
abstract: >-
  Single-nucleus RNA-seq characterization of the dorsolateral, contralaterally-projecting
  glutamatergic population of the mouse Anterior Olfactory Nucleus (AON). An in-house 10x
  snRNA-seq library is paired with the Allen Brain Cell Atlas (MERFISH + 10x Whole Mouse
  Brain) as a spatial and genome-wide reference. Projection status is not measured. A
  dorsolateral position is used as a spatial proxy for projection identity, examined through
  candidate marker genes rather than asserted. Two spatial axes are reported for what each
  measures. Dorsolateral versus ventromedial is the projection-relevant contrast (primary),
  and anteroposterior is the stronger overall molecular axis (a robustness check). Donor-level
  pseudobulk DESeq2 on the Allen ABC Atlas cohort provides the differential-expression result.
  In-house clustering and annotation rest on the single AON library.
type: software
